    <name>hitorro-mesh-pipelines-sqlite</name>
    <description>
        Read-only SQLite source for hitorro-mesh-pipelines. Registered via
        ServiceLoader (SourceAdapter) — dropping this jar on the classpath
        enables `{kind: sqlite, path: "...", query: "SELECT ..."}` in any
        job spec. Turns any local SQLite database (Mac Mail, Photos,
        Messages, Safari history, application caches) into a first-class
        pipeline source, immediately composable with every downstream
        step + sink the pipelines runtime provides.

        Read-only by design — opens the DB with `mode=ro` in the JDBC URL
        so nothing the pipeline runs can mutate the source file. No
        sink counterpart shipped; write-into-SQLite has no obvious
        general semantics and Mail-DB-shaped sources are read-only-forever
        anyway.

        Sources declared with `kind: sqlite` execute driver-local only
        (PipelineScheduler rejects them on the /run-distributed path —
        the DB file lives on the driver host, not on remote agents).

        Dependencies: org.xerial:sqlite-jdbc (self-contained, no JNI).
    </description>

